/Title (Random Forest  K-Means Clustering  Train and evaluate models using parameters such as Nitrogen \(N\),  Phosphorous \(P\), Potassium \(K\), temperature, humidity, pH level, and  rainfall. Select the best-performing model and save it in .pkl format  for deployment.  3. Core Backend Development  Develop the backend system using Flask and modular Python  functions.  Build modules for:  Data preprocessing and cleaning  Model training and evaluation  Crop recommendation prediction  Input validation and preprocessing  The backend processes user input values and generates intelligent  crop recommendations using the trained machine learning model.  4. Data Processing & Model Persistence  Implement preprocessing techniques for handling missing values,  feature scaling, and categorical transformations.  Store the trained machine learning model using Pickle \(.pkl\) for reuse  during prediction.  Maintain datasets and processed outputs for future agricultural  analysis and model improvements.  5. Flask Frontend UI Development  Design an interactive and responsive web interface using HTML,  CSS, and Bootstrap.  Create input forms for agricultural parameters such as:)
